vendor-de/
vendor-sdk/
.venv/
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/cache/
.chroma/
data/index/
# All protected-corpus files stay local EXCEPT (a) the ingestion summary: pure counts/latency/
# fingerprints (no values, no PII), the UI's Replay Ingest stage reads it on a fresh clone; and
# (b) the token manifest: token-ONLY (no clear values), which the serving guardrail's
# surrogate-discount needs — committed so a fresh clone + `docker build` ships it without first
# running a local ingest (else the container's token set is empty and safe replies get withheld).
data/protected/*
!data/protected/ingestion_summary.json
!data/protected/token-manifest.json
*.log

# Telemetry and response caches — never committed.
#
# The result JSONs in data/eval/ ARE committable: they are what docs/results.md verifies
# against, and they carry no clear identifiers (prompts are deliberately not serialized into
# eval results; hybrid provenance prompts contain only protected values at protecting scopes).
# The exclusions below are the leak paths around them: LLM caches hold raw completions —
# including, at scope `none`, model reasoning over clear narratives — and mlruns holds the
# tracking database plus logged artifacts. None of it belongs in a repository whose thesis is
# that sensitive data stays controlled.
docker/observability/mlflow/store/
data/llm_cache/
data/eval/**/llm_cache/
vendor/

# --no-llm smoke outputs. Written under a distinct `-ranking` suffix precisely so they can
# never clobber a paid artifact; they are 500KB of reproducible-for-free duplication and do
# not belong in history.
data/eval/*-ranking.json
data/eval/**/*-ranking.json
# Live-batch run isolation dir: holds fresh LLM outputs from UI-triggered runs.
data/eval/_live/
# Judge caches carry completions the same way llm caches do.
data/eval/**/judge_cache/
# Graph-feature disk memo — pure derived data, rebuilt on demand.
data/cache/
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Internal working materials: kept local, never pushed to the public repo ─────
# Slide decks, presenter script, and the submission email draft.
deck/
# The demo recording script stays local with the other presenter materials.
docs/demo-video-flow.md
# The full engineering decision log is internal; public docs describe decisions inline.
docs/adr/
# Agent/team working agreements and internal vocabulary.
CLAUDE.md
docs/CONTEXT.md
# OS and runtime junk.
.DS_Store
data/.protometer.lock

# Runtime reveal-audit ledgers (hash-chained detokenization records; regenerated at runtime).
data/audit/
data/eval/_attack_reveal_ledger.jsonl
*.egg-info/
